    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d430">

                <pb facs="0633" n="533" sameAs="frus:frus1934v02/pg533"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">868.51 War Credits/650</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Great Britain</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Atherton</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 444</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1934-01-19">January 19, 1934</date>.<lb/>[Received January
                        26.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to the Embassy’s despatch No. 391
                    of December 19<anchor n="2" xml:id="d430-f1"/> with respect to the agreement
                    announced on November 17, 1933, concerning the external indebtedness of Greece,
                    between representatives of the Greek Government, the League Loans Committee
                    (London) and the Council of Foreign Bondholders, I understand that no actual
                    payment has yet been made to the bondholders of the Greek Government 6%
                    stabilization and refugee loan of 1928. At the Embassy’s request, however,
                    Hambros Bank Limited, 41 Bishopsgate, London, E. C. 2, has agreed to forward it
                    a copy of any notice relative to the partial payment of the coupons of this
                    loan, whenever it is in a position to do so.</p>
                <p>As of interest in this connection there is enclosed a copy of an article from the
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Times</hi> of January 19<anchor n="3"
                        xml:id="d430-f2"/> on the subject of the League loans, written by Sir Austen
                    Chamberlain, Chairman of the League Loans Committee (London).</p>
                <p>Respectfully yours,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Ray Atherton</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
